# ---------- new mcq: magnetism ----------
mcq('mag',1,'Outside a bar magnet, magnetic field lines run:','from the north pole to the south pole',['from the south pole to the north pole','from the center outward in all directions','from north pole to north pole'],'Field lines exit N, enter S and form closed loops.')
mcq('mag',1,'Two bar magnets are placed with their north poles facing each other. They will:','repel',['attract','have no force','rotate in place and then attract'],'Like poles repel.')
mcq('mag',1,'Who first reported that a current-carrying wire deflects a compass needle?','Ørsted',['Coulomb','Volta','Ohm'],'Hans Christian Ørsted, 1820, linked electricity and magnetism.')
mcq('mag',2,'Conventional current in a straight wire flows toward you, out of the page. Using the right-hand rule, the magnetic field circles the wire:','counterclockwise',['clockwise','radially outward','parallel to the wire'],'Thumb along the current; fingers curl counterclockwise when the current points out of the page.')
mcq('mag',2,'For a coil, curl the fingers of your right hand in the direction of the current. Your thumb then points toward the coil’s:','north pole',['south pole','center only','side with the lowest voltage'],'Right-hand rule for coils: thumb = north pole.')
mcq('mag',1,'Which change would make an electromagnet stronger?','winding more turns on the same core',['using less current','replacing the iron core with plastic','using a shorter piece of wire for the loops'],'Field strength rises with turns, current and a soft iron core.')
mcq('mag',2,'A key advantage of an electromagnet over a permanent magnet is that it:','can be switched off or adjusted',['never needs power','is always stronger','works without a core'],'Turning the current off or changing it controls the field.')
mcq('mag',1,'A DC motor converts:','electrical energy to mechanical energy',['mechanical energy to electrical energy','heat directly to light','chemical energy to charge'],'A generator does the reverse.')
mcq('mag',2,'Moving a magnet in and out of a coil of wire produces:','a voltage across the coil',['static charge on the magnet','a permanent magnet in the coil','no effect unless the coil is open'],'Changing flux induces an emf (Faraday).')
mcq('mag',2,'Which change increases the voltage induced in a coil by a moving magnet?','moving the magnet faster',['holding the magnet still inside','using fewer turns','replacing the magnet with copper'],'Induced voltage rises with the rate of change of flux and with turns.')
mcq('mag',2,'A transformer needs AC, not steady DC, because:','it needs a changing magnetic field to induce voltage',['DC cannot pass through wire coils','its iron core blocks DC','AC has a higher voltage than DC'],'Steady DC makes constant flux and no induced voltage.')
mcq('mag',2,'A step-up transformer has:','more turns on the secondary than on the primary',['more turns on the primary than on the secondary','equal turns on both','no secondary winding'],'Vs/Vp = Ns/Np.')
mcq('mag',3,'An ideal transformer steps 120 V down to 12 V. Compared with the primary current, the secondary current is:','10 times larger',['10 times smaller','the same','100 times larger'],'Power in = power out, so current rises as voltage falls.')
mcq('mag',2,'The north-seeking end of a compass needle points toward Earth’s geographic north because that region behaves like a magnet’s:','south pole',['north pole','equator','neutral zone'],'Opposite poles attract.')
mcq('mag',2,'The tesla is the SI unit of:','magnetic flux density',['electric charge','capacitance','power'],'1 T = 1 N/(A·m).')
mcq('mag',1,'Which of these is strongly attracted to a magnet?','nickel',['copper','aluminum','gold'],'Iron, nickel and cobalt are ferromagnetic.')
mcq('hist',1,'Who discovered electromagnetic induction?','Faraday',['Ohm','Volta','Kirchhoff'],'Michael Faraday, 1831.')
mcq('hist',2,'The unit of capacitance is named for:','Faraday',['Tesla','Volta','Hertz'],'1 farad = 1 coulomb per volt.')
mcq('hist',2,'Tesla is best known in electrical engineering for:','alternating-current power systems',['the first chemical battery','the law of force between charges','the algebra of logic'],'Tesla developed the AC induction motor and polyphase AC.')
